# GLM 4.5 Flash — findings by Qwen 3.8 Max (SELF-EXCLUDED)

- Source: Z.ai (`z-ai/glm-4.5-flash` / `opencode/glm-4.5-flash`; free tier of the GLM-4.5 family; **no AA page (404) / no benchmark-aggregator coverage (benchlm 404) / no Flash-specific benchmark published by Z.ai**)
- Date: 2026-11-01 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **Verdict — SELF-EXCLUDED.** **GLM-4.5-Flash** is a **real, named, dated artifact** — the **free API-only tier** of Z.ai's GLM-4.5 family (model id `glm-4.5-flash`, released **2025-07-28**, **128K ctx / 96K max output**, **text-only**, **hybrid thinking/non-thinking**, native function calling, Claude-Code/Roo-Code compatible) — but it has **no measurement of its own anywhere**. Scoring is impossible under the no-reattribution and no-invented-numbers rules because **(a) Artificial Analysis returns 404 for `glm-4-5-flash`** (no Intelligence Index / Speed / Cost), **(b) the benchmark aggregator benchlm also 404s** (no independent cell), and **(c) Z.ai publishes NO Flash-specific benchmark numbers** — its 12-suite averages (**GLM-4.5 = 63.2 / GLM-4.5-Air = 59.8**) belong to the **stronger paid flagship and Air siblings**, not the free Flash. The curated `meta` describes it only qualitatively ("free lightweight … robust tool-calling") and its own tradeoff admits a **"lighter distilled parameter footprint relative to flagship GLM-4.5 … lower headroom on multi-file SWE-bench tasks"** — yet attaches **no score**. Any numeric rating would require either **inventing numbers** or **reattributing the flagship/Air benchmarks onto a deliberately weaker free serving tier**, which would *overstate* it. The entry is therefore **excluded, not scored** — the same reasoning that excluded **`glm-4.6-flash`**.

## Why this is a self-exclusion (not a scored model)

- **It is a free *serving tier*, not a separately benchmarked checkpoint.** Every source frames `glm-4.5-flash` as *"the free tier in Z.ai's GLM-4.5 model family … shares the hybrid reasoning architecture of the broader GLM-4.5 series"* (Puter) and *"Flash is the free tier"* of the five-text-model family (glm-ai.chat). Z.ai's own launch page lists it under capability tags — *"Free · Strong Performance · Excellent for Reasoning, Coding & Agents"* — with **no evaluation row**. It is a no-cost endpoint (`$0/$0` on the Z.ai platform), not a model with published scores.
- **No independent tracker has ever measured it.** **`artificialanalysis.ai/models/glm-4-5-flash` → 404** (contrast: the **GLM-4.5 flagship** has a full AA page). **`benchlm.ai/models/glm-4-5-flash` → 404** (no aggregated cell). There is no leaderboard entry, Vals run, or third-party reproduction under the `glm-4.5-flash` name.
- **The only numbers in circulation belong to *other* models.** The "87.0 AIME 2025 / 67.9 SWE-Bench Verified" that surfaces near the Flash in search snippets is drawn from a **different model's card** on the same aggregator list, not from the Flash; the real family figures Z.ai reports (**GLM-4.5 avg 63.2, GLM-4.5-Air avg 59.8, SWE / Terminal / TAU / BFCL suites**) are the **355B/32B flagship** and **106B/12B Air** results. Crediting those to the free, lighter Flash would be **reattribution** — and, per the `meta` ("lower headroom"), **an overstatement**.
- **Contrast with the sibling that WAS scored.** **`glm-4.7-flash`** (scored separately) had a **Flash-branded vendor benchmark table** (SWE-bench Verified 59.2, τ²-Bench 79.5, AIME-2025 91.6, GPQA 75.2, LiveCodeBench v6 64.0, BrowseComp 42.8) transcribed by RITS/NYU from Z.ai's own GLM-4.7-Flash release material. **`glm-4.5-flash` has no analogous Flash-specific table** — so the same evidentiary bar that justified scoring 4.7-Flash is *absent* here. The distinction is measurement availability, not vendor.

## What we did establish (documented, not scored)

- **Identity & lifecycle:** a genuine Z.ai model id **`glm-4.5-flash`**, **released 2025-07-28** alongside the GLM-4.5 family, positioned as the **free** sibling of GLM-4.5 (355B/32B), **GLM-4.5-Air** (106B/12B), GLM-4.5-X, and GLM-4.5-AirX; later **superseded as the free pick by GLM-4.7-Flash** (and the GLM-5.x Flash line).
- **Verified specs (aggregators, consistent):** **text in → text out** (no vision), **128K context**, **96K max output**, **hybrid thinking (toggleable) + non-thinking instant modes**, **native function calling / structured output / streaming**, **$0 input / $0 output** on the Z.ai developer platform, Claude-Code / Roo-Code integration.
- **Qualitative standing (vendor framing only, unquantified):** marketed for *"prototypes and hobby projects … cost-sensitive agent workflows,"* explicitly with *"lower headroom"* than the flagship on multi-file coding — **but never expressed as a number.**

> **Consistency check:** this is the **variant-with-no-own-measurement** pattern — the same reasoning used to exclude **`glm-4.6-flash`** ("no published Flash-specific benchmarks; Z.ai publishes flagship numbers only") and **`ling-3.0-flash-sante`**. It is **not** like **`glm-4.7-flash`**, which is *scored* precisely because a **Flash-branded benchmark table exists**. **No dimension scores are assigned**, and **no GLM-4.5 / GLM-4.5-Air numbers are transferred onto this label.**

